# install.mjs embeds skills/ and hooks/ as a single-line base64 payload, so the
# decoded bytes carry whatever line endings existed on the machine that ran
# `npm run build`. If a checkout converts those files to CRLF, two things break:
# the installed copy no longer matches the repo source, and the next build on
# that machine re-embeds CRLF and produces a different install.mjs than the one
# committed. Forcing LF everywhere keeps the build byte-reproducible across
# Linux, macOS and Windows.
#
# Caught by the byte-identical assertion in scripts/test-install.mjs, which
# failed on windows-latest while passing on every other runner.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never convert.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
